# Transsion's camera file-lock manager. Stock ships it, labels it and runs it;
# device/mediatek/sepolicy_vndr has no domain for it, so on this tree the binary
# stayed u:object_r:vendor_file:s0 and init could never transition into it —
# the service has therefore NEVER started on any build of this ROM.
#
# The visible cost, every boot since build 62, from a healthy camera HAL:
#   avc: denied { find } for
#     interface=vendor.transsion.hardware.trancam.trancamserver::ITrancamserver
#     scontext=u:r:mtk_hal_camera:s0
#     tcontext=u:object_r:default_android_hwservice:s0 tclass=hwservice_manager
#
# 🔑 This is the "a service running is not a service serving" class one step
# earlier still: pnpmgr at least RAN. This one never even started, while the
# tree shipped its binary, its rc and its four libraries — a dead payload that
# looked installed. Same remedy as PNPMGR (build 77): carry stock's own labels,
# under the same rule — SHIPPED provider AND measured denial, both satisfied.
#
# Stock's labels, for the record:
#   .build/work/vendor/etc/selinux/vendor_file_contexts:275
#     /(system\/vendor|vendor)/bin/hw/vendor.transsion.hardware.trancam.trancamserver@1.0-service
#       u:object_r:trancamserver_exec:s0
#   .build/work/vendor/etc/selinux/vendor_hwservice_contexts:68
#     vendor.transsion.hardware.trancam.trancamserver::ITrancamserver
#       u:object_r:hal_trancamserver_hwservice:s0
#
# ✅ MEASURED ON HARDWARE (build 77) BEFORE THIS WAS WRITTEN — the closure ships
# and the daemon is healthy, so this is not a policy for a binary that cannot run:
#   every DT_NEEDED resolves (libcutils, liblog, libhidlbase, libutils, libc++
#     and its own @1.0.so — all four libs and trancam_filelock.json are on the
#     device)
#   run by hand it logged "TRANCAM_DEBUG: Trancamserver", REGISTERED
#     ITrancamserver/default, and stayed up as a daemon
#   with the find granted, `lshal` showed it serving (server-pid column Y),
#     the camera HAL restarted clean, 2 camera devices still enumerated,
#     the providers still registered, 0 FATAL and 0 tombstones
# 🔴 BUILD 78 BROKE THE CAMERA WITH THIS FILE. Read this before touching it.
#
# The first version of this domain used init_daemon_domain + add_hwservice and
# hand-written binder_call rules, derived by grepping stock's compiled CIL for
# "trancamserver". That method can only see rules that name the domain DIRECTLY,
# and it is BLUEPRINT section 9's documented trap verbatim:
# **attribute-mediated grants are invisible to a grep for the domain name.**
#
# What it missed, all of it from ONE attribute (private/halserverdomain.te):
#     hwbinder_use(halserverdomain)                     the call to hwservicemanager
#     get_prop(halserverdomain, hwservicemanager_prop)  used to WAIT for it
#     allow halserverdomain system_file:dir r_dir_perms
#
# So trancamserver started, could not read hwservicemanager_prop, could not call
# hwservicemanager, and never registered -- while init.svc said `running`.
#
# 🔴 AND THAT WAS NOT COSMETIC, because the interface was now LABELLED.
# Before build 78 camerahalserver's getService() on ITrancamserver was DENIED and
# returned null, which the camera tolerated. With a label the find is PERMITTED,
# so getService() instead entered a blocking retry:
#     HidlServiceManagement: Waited one second for ...ITrancamserver/default
#     hwservicemanager: ...not registered, trying to start it as a lazy HAL
#     libc: Unable to set property "ctl.interface_start" ... error 0x20
# camerahalserver never registered ICameraProvider ->
#     dumpsys media.camera -> "Number of camera devices: 0"
# RESUME says this exact thing about build 68: **a DECLARED interface that never
# registers is a BOOT HANG, not a degraded feature.** A half-fixed HAL is worse
# than an unfixed one; the label and a working server must land together.
#
# FIXED by joining the ATTRIBUTE stock joins, rather than copying the three rules
# it currently expands to -- enumerating an attribute inherits nothing later.
# Verified in stock's own CIL: typeattributeset halserverdomain (... trancamserver
# ...), plus hal_trancamserver / hal_trancamserver_server.
#
# ✅ BOTH HALVES PROVEN ON HARDWARE (build 78, live via ksud sepolicy patch,
# instrument controlled -- the hwservicemanager_prop denial rate went from ~110
# per 12 s to 0, which is the control):
#     trancamserver  ->  lshal server-pid Y, ITrancamserver/default REGISTERED
#     camera         ->  "Number of camera devices: 2", providers @2.4/@2.5/@2.6
#                        all registered and serving again
hal_attribute(trancamserver)

type trancamserver, domain;
type trancamserver_exec, exec_type, vendor_file_type, file_type;

init_daemon_domain(trancamserver)

# halserverdomain + hal_trancamserver{,_server}. This is the line whose absence
# broke the camera; do NOT replace it with the rules it happens to expand to.
hal_server_domain(trancamserver, hal_trancamserver)

# Publish its own HIDL interface. Without the hwservice type the name falls to
# default_android_hwservice, which a vendor domain may neither add nor find —
# the exact shape of the PNPMGR vndservice bug.
add_hwservice(trancamserver, hal_trancamserver_hwservice)

# The one measured client. Stock ALSO grants cameraserver and system_server the
# find plus a binder_call, and those are deliberately NOT carried here: both are
# platform domains, neither has ever produced a denial for this interface on any
# build of this tree, and granting a core domain access to a vendor service with
# no evidence it asks is how dead policy accumulates. If either ever asks, it
# will say so in an avc record and can be added with a measurement behind it.
allow mtk_hal_camera hal_trancamserver_hwservice:hwservice_manager find;
binder_call(mtk_hal_camera, trancamserver)
binder_call(trancamserver, mtk_hal_camera)
